WEBVTT

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:07.973
Neurodiversity describes the
idea that people experience

00:00:07.998 --> 00:00:10.770
and interact with the world
around them in different ways.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.470
There is no one right way of thinking,
learning, and behaving, and these

00:00:15.471 --> 00:00:17.610
differences are not to be viewed as
deficits.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.475
It's important for
all of us to foster an

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.191
environment that is
conducive to neurodiversity.

00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:27.810
We need to recognize and emphasize each
and every person's individual strengths

00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:31.630
and talents, and provide support for their
differences and requirements.

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:35.163
People with neurological
differences are not

00:00:35.164 --> 00:00:38.151
broken or incomplete
versions of normal people.

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:40.630
We're all born different
and raised differently.

00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:44.502
Hence, all of us are to
some extent differently abled.

00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:49.392
Neurodiversity is a normal and natural
variation in the human genome.

00:00:50.236 --> 00:00:52.319
The distinctiveness of
neurodiverse people isn't

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.131
something that necessarily
needs to be cured.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.999
Neurodiverse employees merely
need some help and accommodation.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.771
They may bring new
perspectives to an

00:01:01.772 --> 00:01:04.671
organization's efforts to
create or recognize value.

00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:08.803
In this course, you will
recognize the value that

00:01:08.804 --> 00:01:11.511
neurodiverse employees
add to an organization.

00:01:12.045 --> 00:01:14.787
You'll understand how to
educate your employees about

00:01:14.812 --> 00:01:17.951
neurodiversity and create
an inclusive workplace.

00:01:18.365 --> 00:01:20.633
You'll learn to examine
strategies for providing

00:01:20.645 --> 00:01:23.115
equal access to
neurodiverse employees.